      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8ee07ed5-35eb-54a9-97aa-04cddee85a93",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cave Rock Tunnel, Stateline, Nevada, Lake Tahoe, Douglas County, Nevada, Cave Rock\n- Roads: U.S. Route 50\n- Peoples: Washoe, Paiute\n- Concepts: Tahoe Tessie\n\nFacts:\n- In the mid-19th century, members of the Washoe and Paiute tribes told stories that Tahoe Tessie lived in an underwater tunnel beneath Cave Rock.\n- Sightings of Tahoe Tessie have continued into modern times.\n- Cave Rock Tunnel is a dual-bore highway tunnel on U.S. Route 50 along the eastern shore of Lake Tahoe about seven miles north of Stateline in Douglas County, Nevada, United States.\n- Stateline, Nevada, had a population of 842 at the 2010 census.",
